Changes from the original, made in 2026 by Nexa:
- Renamed to Nexa Agent (bundle identifier app.nexa.agent), with the
  Nexa icon, palette and accent colour, and Simplified Chinese by default.
- Watches Claude Code and Codex only; no data is read and no hooks or
  observers are installed for any other client.
- Docked HUDs can float anywhere on the desktop and remember the spot,
  snapping onto an edge when dropped close to it; a floating HUD opens
  from where it stands.
- Finds the Claude desktop app's own Claude Code engine.
- Reply reminders show the whole reply and answer the session from the
  card: Codex Desktop starts the turn itself over its local IPC, other
  Codex threads and Claude Code sessions are resumed in the background.
  The panel's session rows open the same quick chat on demand.
- Builds with the Xcode Command Line Tools alone (no SwiftUI @Entry macro).
